 "defect_observations": [
  "Body lines 11-13 (chapter introduction) say a reduction preserves the information exactly when it is sufficient, without the finiteness condition that thm:p15-w02b-p15-045-reduction(3)-(4) shows is necessary; the sentence is attributed to the source, but a reader may take it as the chapter's claim.",
  "def:p15-w02b-p15-045-grouping (body lines 614-627) says the source's printed r=2 value .0903 is half the value of its own formula (6.2) (0.18062), so the best grouping changes. Printed table (6.6) on p. 85 and the conclusion on p. 86 match the quotation; the recomputation 0.3 log10 1.6 + 0.3 log10 2.5 = 0.18062 checks. Not a coverage defect.",
  "thm:p15-w02b-p15-045-footnote(2) gives quadrature decimals (log k ~ 1.907, I(2:1) ~ 0.430) that the annex does not derive; annex lines 586-589 say they are not used in any argument. Not checked.",
  "No placeholder text found in the owned files. The density-criterion proof (annex lines 276-341) and fact (P) are self-contained and do not rely on Halmos-Savage.",
  "Source-extent gap recorded on section 166.4 as duty X-source-extent: The packet's source extent for ED26-METHOD-relative-information is the complete Kullback-Leibler 1951 article and its stated information/sufficiency results. Three stated results are referenced but not reconstructed in the owned files: (a) the expansion (2.7)-(2.9), p. 81, relating I(1:2) and J(1,2) between neighbouring parameter values to Fisher's information (body lines 686-693 decline to state it because the source lists no hypotheses; it is not stated with explicitly supplied exact hypotheses and proved); (b) the general k-variate normal divergence formula (2.10), p. 81-82 (J(1,2) equal to k times Mahalanobis' generalized distance), of which only the case k=1 is computed (thm:p15-w02b-p15-045-not-metric, body lines 432-443); (c) the Section 6(1) Lehmann critical-region computation (6.1), p. 85, comparing I_{1:2}(G) with I_{1:2}(F), mentioned only in prose at body lines 494-496."
 ],
